      "message": "\u003e Hi Mark, \n\ns/k/c/\n\n\u003e do you mean to try this way ? It looks very hack way. Is this what you are suggesting ? Please share more details. \n\u003e \n\u003e +++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/Makefile\n\u003e @@ -4,7 +4,7 @@\n\u003e  #\n\u003e \n\u003e  asflags-y :\u003d -D__KVM_NVHE_HYPERVISOR__\n\u003e -ccflags-y :\u003d -D__KVM_NVHE_HYPERVISOR__\n\u003e +ccflags-y :\u003d -D__KVM_NVHE_HYPERVISOR__ -D__DISABLE_CONFIG_TRACE_RW__\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e diff --git a/include/linux/iorw.h b/include/linux/iorw.h\n\u003e index bab641e..7c2629e 100644\n\u003e --- a/include/linux/iorw.h\n\u003e +++ b/include/linux/iorw.h\n\u003e @@ -9,7 +9,7 @@\n\u003e  #include \u003clinux/atomic.h\u003e\n\u003e  #include \u003clinux/tracepoint-defs.h\u003e\n\u003e \n\u003e -#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_TRACE_RW)\n\u003e +#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_TRACE_RW) \u0026\u0026 !(defined(__DISABLE_CONFIG_TRACE_RW__))\n\nNo, that looks horrible. We currently disable tracing in the EL2 object by removing CC_FLAGS_FTRACE in the Makefile. Why isn\u0027t that enough in your case? It seems to indicate that you are bypassing some other guards and not obeying the notrace attribute.",
