      "message": "Marc probably knows a better way to inhibit the trace definitions based on CC_FLAGS_FTRACE, but this will build if you remove all of the changes to this file and make the iorw logging macros contingent on !IS_DEFINED(__KVM_NVHE_HYPERVISOR__) in include/linux/iorw.h:\n\n```\ndiff --git a/include/linux/iorw.h b/include/linux/iorw.h\nindex bab641e91d2b7..15ce9ea846c85 100644\n--- a/include/linux/iorw.h\n+++ b/include/linux/iorw.h\n@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@\n #include \u003clinux/atomic.h\u003e\n #include \u003clinux/tracepoint-defs.h\u003e\n \n-#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_TRACE_RW)\n+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_TRACE_RW) \u0026\u0026 !IS_ENABLED(__KVM_NVHE_HYPERVISOR__)\n DECLARE_TRACEPOINT(rwio_writeb);\n DECLARE_TRACEPOINT(rwio_writew);\n DECLARE_TRACEPOINT(rwio_writel);\n```\n\nMarc, suggestions how to do this correctly?",
